              "done": true,
              "tool": "shell",
              "input": {
                "command": "cat main.go"
              },
              "output": "main() switches on os.Args[1]. build calls Site.Build(); serve uses http.FileServer for public/.",
              "seq": 8
            },
            {
              "at": 1794318664531,
              "id": "14e8881b:answer2",
              "kind": "text",
              "done": true,
              "text": "`main()` dispatches on the first command-line argument:\n\n- **`build`** creates a `Site` with the content, template, and output directories, then calls `Build()`. It prints how many pages were built.\n- **`serve`** parses the preview address and serves `public/`.\n- A missing or unknown command prints a usage message or error and exits.\n\nThe rendering work lives in `build.go`, not in this command dispatcher. Notice the call to `site.Build()` in the file beside this conversation.\n\n**No files changed and no tests were run.**",
              "seq": 9
            },
